The attached image, Figure 6 from the PDF, demonstrates that Nano-11 enhances the expression of costimulatory molecules on dendritic cells (DCs). Flow cytometry histograms show that after two days of incubation, DCs treated with 250 µg/mL Nano-11 (black line) exhibit a marked increase in surface expression of CD40, CD80, and CD86 compared to untreated control cells (gray line). This increased expression indicates the activation of DCs, a critical step for Nano-11 to function as an effective vaccine adjuvant and promote a robust immune response.